# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; this template is not.
#
# Cloudflare Realtime TURN, from dash.cloudflare.com -> Realtime -> TURN.
# "App ID" in that dashboard is the key id that goes in the credentials URL.
# The API token is shown once, at creation.
#
# Both are optional. Without them the credentials endpoint answers 503, the app
# falls back to STUN alone, and every room that could connect directly still
# does -- which is most of them. TURN only rescues the pairs that cannot, and
# those are the ones a symmetric NAT has already made impossible.
#
# Set the same two names in Netlify's environment for the deployed site.
TURN_KEY_ID=
TURN_KEY_API_TOKEN=
